  "capture_notes": "Actual Orient/Orient3Pt commands transform four authored noncoplanar witnesses. The local producer runs real registered commands from original source/reference/target recipes, with no returned native matrices or geometry as inputs. Group counts include only active definitions owned by the probe. The initial worker failed because IronPython lacks math.isfinite; its diagnostic is retained and excluded. Helpers evolved during discovery, so final hashes are reproducer fingerprints rather than proof of identical staged bytes for every earlier capture.",
  "cancellation_return_policy": "Completed workflows require successful RunScript return. The local producer explicitly marks requested cancellation false. Rhino returned true when Orient3Pt was canceled at its third target, with unchanged model geometry. Cancellation recipes compare model points, identity, selection and group counts independently of that native diagnostic boolean; no script-return parity is claimed for cancellation.",
  "numerical_notes": "Rhino accepted 1e-8 reference/target spacing at 1e-6 model tolerance, exposing the old model-tolerance rejection. Exact opposite directions exposed the generic rotation helper's different fallback axis; point commands now reuse the existing OpenNURBS normal-frame perpendicular policy. Nearly opposite directions retain their cross-product axis. No new native ABI or proprietary implementation was used.",
  "limitations": [
    "Near-collinear and extreme-coordinate frames remain unqualified.",
    "Native grip workflows, multiple whole-source group ordering, native Undo/Redo, rendered appearance and general performance are not established by these captures.",
    "Scale state is outside model Undo. Interactive accepted option changes are remembered on cancellation; rejected complete commands preserve their previous scale state.",
    "The native RunScript cancellation result is a diagnostic, with the recorded third-target exception described above."
  ],
